  "observations": [
    "Managed subscribe validates the actual installed SIP adapter, source binding/lifecycle, exact managed controller and principal. Source publication captures ReceivedDtmfDisclosure before try_send into its bounded queue. The metadata retains original closed audiences and source incarnation, not domain permission readers or native signing facts.",
    "A monotonic scene boundary is advanced after committed audience/member mutations under membership custody. Earlier, equal-boundary or future physical timestamps cannot acquire a later audience. Busy/stale managed capture increments drop counters; it is never reexecuted later under a new audience. Source registration replacement and binding epochs retain their existing invalidation behavior.",
    "The received-to-native audience fence owns the SIP source managed credential during each real IO callback. Native target physical custody supplies its credential; it is not reentered. Original/current group and current member checks surround IO and release all synchronous guards on Pending. Actual host source/recipient permission and actual SIP source/native target physical fences remain separate mandatory custody.",
    "Seven new controlled scene methods are included in the56method privacy suite; they are not counted a second time. Existing declaration exact-credential/revision/no-port-change and source binding epoch checks each pass once. All17actual native DTMF and2two-call native-to-SIP fanout methods pass after the Core refactor.",
    "The new isolated actual Connect fixture uses the signed public client for Session invite/native setup, an actual configured answered SIP leg and negotiated RTP. A test-support-only accessor returns the actual installed adapter managed source subscription. It grants no delivery or media/signal permission. Actual INFO digest andRFC4733SSRC0x87654321/PT101/8kHz/1896samples/start-observed facts retain237ms without relabeling or clamping. Re-registering ends the original subscription; native_dtmf_sources remains empty, and original duplex thresholds and BYE/retired-answer cleanup still pass.",
    "Captured source facts are private diagnostic records, not a newly supported HTTP/SDK DTO or independent SIP signature verification. EdDSA/ES256 cover the configured Connect native control composition; SIP input is the actual isolated UDP fixture."
  ],
